<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Qalawun</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Qalawun was a sultan of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk-sultanate">Mamluk Sultanate</a> in the late thirteenth century and founder of a dynasty that ruled for about a century. His campaigns continued the work of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/baybars">Baybars</a> against the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusader states</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a>. His descendants included <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/al-nasir-muhammad">al-Nasir Muhammad</a>, under whom <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> power reached its height.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/qalawun.jpg" alt="Qalawun" width="270" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Ahmed zakaria 2025 · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%D9%82%D8%A8%D8%A9_%D8%B6%D8%B1%D9%8A%D8%AD_%D8%A7%D9%84%D8%B3%D9%84%D8%B7%D8%A7%D9%86_%D8%A7%D9%84%D9%85%D9%85%D9%84%D9%88%D9%83%D9%8A_%D9%82%D9%84%D8%A7%D9%88%D9%88%D9%86.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
